# Target C — C75 rhombus diagonal-slack capacity frontier

**LEVEL I STATUS: STILL OPEN.**

Full proof: [target_c_rhombus_diagonal_slack_capacity_2026-08-31.md](../../reports/target_c_rhombus_diagonal_slack_capacity_2026-08-31.md).

C49 charged every strict unit-rhombus face only by the limiting area
`sqrt(3)/2`. C75 retains the amount of strictness.

If `s_f in (1,sqrt(2)]` is the short diagonal of a bounded unit-rhombus contact face,
then

`area(f)=(1/2)s_f sqrt(4-s_f^2)`.

This function is concave on `[1,sqrt(2)]`. Therefore

`area(f)-sqrt(3)/2 >= c_rh(s_f-1)`,

where

`c_rh=(1-sqrt(3)/2)/(sqrt(2)-1)=0.32344...`.

Let

`Sigma_diag=sum_(bounded 4-faces)(s_f-1)`.

C42's face count and disjoint face interiors give

`m <= (2/sqrt(3))area(F)
      -lambda_rh Sigma_diag
      +5q-3c_I-3e_BB-5`,

with

`lambda_rh=2c_rh/sqrt(3)=0.37348...`.

Hence

`m <= Delta_2 D^2
      -lambda_rh Sigma_diag
      +5pi D-3c_I-3e_BB-5`.

This is a weight-free strict refinement of the whole-hull C49 capacity estimate.

## Fixed diagonal threshold

For `tau>0`, let `N_tau` be the number of rhombic faces with short diagonal at least
`1+tau`. Then

`Sigma_diag>=tau N_tau`,

so

`m <= Delta_2D^2-lambda_rh tau N_tau+5pi D-...`.

If a force-visible core satisfies

`m>=Delta_2D^2-O(D)`,

then

`Sigma_diag=O(D)`

and

`N_tau=O_tau(D)`

for every fixed `tau>0`. More generally `N_(tau_D)=O(D/tau_D)`.

## Interaction with C73

C73 says all but `O(D)` core vertices are degree-four vertices surrounded by four
strict rhombi. Under near-capacity, C75 says all but `O_tau(D)` rhombi have missing
short diagonal below `1+tau`. Therefore all but `O_tau(D)` core vertices lie in a
near-triangular missing-diagonal bulk: four surrounding unit rhombi, every missing
short diagonal in `(1,1+tau)`.

This charges transverse geometry independently of how small its KKT stress is.

## Next target

The exact remaining alternatives are:

1. prove a force-bulk estimate controlling `n-m`, so the C75 core-capacity penalty
   transfers to the whole source; or
2. prove a finite perturbation/stability theorem excluding a contact-minimal global
   minimizer with a quadratic near-triangular missing-diagonal rhombic bulk.